# Ignore rules for pyserve, gitignore style.
#
# The last rule that matches an entry wins, so a '!' rule placed after a broader
# rule brings that entry back into view.
#
# A rule containing a '/' is anchored to the served root, exactly as in
# gitignore, so '__pycache__/*' would only ever match at the top level. Write
# '__pycache__/' instead to hide the folder wherever it turns up.

.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
